        "original_id": "b84cf921-e3ba-5ece-b13e-7dda6b32def7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dziga Vertov, Roger Donaldson\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, cinema theorist\n- Places: Soviet Union, Australia, New Zealand, United States\n- Products: The World's Fastest Indian, Smash Palace, No Way Out, Dante's Peak, Thirteen Days\n\nFacts:\n- Dziga Vertov was born as David Abelevich Kaufman, was also known as Denis Kaufman, and lived from 2 January 1896 to 12 February 1954.\n- Dziga Vertov was a Soviet pioneer documentary film director, newsreel director, and cinema theorist.\n- Roger Donaldson was born on 15 November 1945 and is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer, and writer.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the acclaimed 1981 relationship drama Smash Palace.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the Kevin Costner film No Way Out in 1987.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the disaster film Dante's Peak in 1997.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the Kevin Costner film Thirteen Days in 2000.\n- Roger Donaldson's films include The World's Fastest Indian, released in 2005.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
